# audit.local.txt — YOUR identifiers for `make audit`, kept on your machine.
#
# `make audit` already derives your coordinates from the resolved configuration
# (kit/gsvtk-config minus the shipped defaults), so this file is usually empty. Add a
# line for anything private that config does not name: a hostname, a personal directory
# that is not $GSVTK_WORK, initials, a colleague's username, a lab-internal bucket.
#
# Copy to `audit.local.txt` (gitignored) and fill it in.

# A literal, matched case-insensitively, one per line:
#   <your-machine-hostname>
#   <your-initials>

# A regex, prefixed with `re:` (matched case-insensitively):
#   re:\b[a-z]+-[a-z]+-[0-9]{4,}\b        # e.g. your workspace-name convention

# Declare a derived value public so it stops being flagged:
#   waive all_samples
